\displaystyle \frac1{x_{2025}}+1=M .
\end{cases}
\]

From \(\frac1{x_{k}}+x_{k+1}=M\) we obtain the recurrence  

\[
x_{k+1}=M-\frac1{x_{k}}\qquad(k\ge 1),\qquad x_{1}=M .
\tag{1}
\]

Define the Möbius transformation  

\[
f(t)=M-\frac1t=\frac{Mt-1}{t}.
\]

Writing \(f\) as a matrix  

\[
f(t)=\frac{Mt-1}{t}\;\Longleftrightarrow\;
\begin{pmatrix}M&-1\\[1mm]1&0\end{pmatrix},
\]

its \(n\)-th iterate corresponds to the matrix  

\[
A^{n}=U_{n}A-U_{n-1}I ,
\qquad
U_{0}=0,\;U_{1}=1,\;U_{n+1}=MU_{n}-U_{n-1}.
\tag{2}
\]

Applying \(f\) \(2024\) times to the initial value \(M\) gives  

\[
x_{2025}=f^{2024}(M)=\frac{U_{2024}M^{2}-U_{2023}M-U_{2024}}
{U_{2024}M-U_{2023}}
      =\frac{U_{2024}(M^{2}-1)-U_{2023}M}{U_{2025}} .
\]

The last required equality is  

\[
\frac1{x_{2025}}+1=M\quad\Longrightarrow\quad x_{2025}=\frac1{M-1}.
\]

Hence  

\[
\frac{U_{2024}M^{2}-U_{2023}M-U_{2024}}{U_{2025}}=\frac1{M-1}.
\tag{3}
\]

