Triggers: show k objects exist with property, greedy algorithm existence, select points no three collinear
Technique: Greedy existence proof: grab objects one at a time satisfying property. When stuck with n objects, count how many were BLOCKED by each chosen object. If each blocks at most f(n) others, then n+n·f(n)≥total, giving n≥total/(1+f(n)). Example: from 4951 points, greedily select no-three-collinear. Each point blocks ≤C(n,2)/2 others, giving 4951-n≤C(n,2), so n≥100.
