--- [number_theory.valuation.padic_valuations] ---
Triggers: track exact prime power in factorials or products, v_p(n!) computation, ultrametric inequality for sums, need to compare powers of p dividing expressions
Technique: p-adic valuation ν_p(n) = max k with p^k|n. Key formulas: (1) Legendre: ν_p(n!) = Σ⌊n/p^i⌋ = (n - s_p(n))/(p-1) where s_p(n) = digit sum in base p. (2) Kummer: ν_p(C(m+n,m)) = number of carries when adding m,n in base p. (3) Ultrametric: ν_p(a+b) ≥ min(ν_p(a),ν_p(b)), with EQUALITY when ν_p(a)≠ν_p(b). TRAP: when ν_p(a)=ν_p(b), cancellation can make ν_p(a+b) arbitrarily large. (4) ν_p(ab) = ν_p(a)+ν_p(b). Use Legendre to compare factorials, Kummer for binomial coefficients.
Question: Find v_2(100!) (the largest power of 2 dividing 100!).
Answer: By Legendre formula: v_2(100!) = floor(100/2) + floor(100/4) + floor(100/8) + floor(100/16) + floor(100/32) + floor(100/64) = 50+25+12+6+3+1 = 97. Alternatively: v_2(100!) = (100 - s_2(100))/(2-1) where s_2(100) = s_2(1100100_2) = 1+1+0+0+1+0+0 = 3, giving (100-3)/1 = 97. Legendre is the standard tool for v_p(n!) and v_p(C(n,k)) computations.

