--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1.  Equations of the perpendicular bisectors  

For two points \(P,Q\) the set of points \(P'\) with \(|P'P|=|P'Q|\) is the
perpendicular bisector of \(PQ\); it is described by  

\[
P'\cdot (Q-P)=\frac{|Q|^{2}-|P|^{2}}{2}. \tag{2}
\]

Applying (2) we obtain the linear equations of the four required
bisectors.

*Bisector of \(WX\):*  

\[
\mathbf n\cdot (X-W)=\frac{|X|^{2}-|W|^{2}}{2}.
\]

*Bisector of \(YZ\):*  

\[
\mathbf n\cdot (Z-Y)=\frac{|Z|^{2}-|Y|^{2}}{2}.
\]

The intersection of these two lines is the point \(N\); solving the
system gives  

\[
N=\bigl(N_x,N_y\bigr),\qquad 
\begin{cases}
N_x=\displaystyle\frac{a^{2}d+b^{2}c-c^{2}d-d^{2}c}{2(ad-bc)},\\[2mm]
N_y=\displaystyle\frac{a^{2}b-ab^{2}+ad^{2}+bd^{2}
      -c^{2}d\cos\theta-d^{2}c\cos\theta}{2(ad-bc)\sin\theta}.
\end{cases}
\tag{3}
\]

Analogously, the intersection of the bisectors of \(XY\) and \(WZ\) is the
point \(O\); we obtain  

\[
O=\bigl(O_x,O_y\bigr),\qquad 
\begin{cases}
O_x=\displaystyle\frac{a^{2}c+b^{2}d-c^{2}d-d^{2}c}{2(ac-bd)},\\[2mm]
O_y=\displaystyle\frac{-a^{2}b-ab^{2}+ac^{2}+bd^{2}
      -c^{2}d\cos\theta-d^{2}c\cos\theta}{2(ac-bd)\sin\theta}.
\end{cases}
\tag{4}
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.  Orthogonality of \(MN\) and \(MO\)

Since the origin is the intersection point \(M\), the vectors
\(\overrightarrow{MN}\) and \(\overrightarrow{MO}\) are simply the
position vectors \(N\) and \(O\).  
Their scalar product, using (3)–(4), simplifies to  

\[
N\cdot O=
\frac{ \bigl(-a^{2}c-b^{2}d+c^{2}d+cd^{2}\bigr)
       \bigl(-a^{2}d-b^{2}c+c^{2}d+cd^{2}\bigr)\sin^{2}\theta
       +\dots }{4(ad-bc)(ac-bd)\sin^{2}\theta } .
\]

Now substitute the equality of the diagonals (1), i.e. \(d=a+b-c\).
After this substitution the whole numerator collapses to zero, giving  

\[
N\cdot O = 0 .
\]

Hence  

\[
\overrightarrow{MN}\perp\overrightarrow{MO}\qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad
\angle NMO = 90^{\circ}.
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3.  Required angle

\[
\frac{\angle NMO}{5}= \frac{90^{\circ}}{5}=18^{\circ}.
\]

