Triangular prism: 1152
```

So a 3‑regular graph with 4 vertices (K₄) has **48** admissible edge‑colourings, while the 6‑vertex triangular prism has **1152** admissible colourings.  These numbers can be used as a sanity check when you later set up a more sophisticated counting method (e.g., using the component‑graph description) for the icosahedron, which has 20 vertices and 30 edges.  The same program can be adapted to the icosahedron once an explicit edge list is supplied.

